Well, I'm making PL7 on an AT&T 3B2 running System V Rel 3.2.2, and
I think my compiler is the CPLU4.2 version.  The make isn't finished
yet, but I've had to fix two problems - unixmain.c and mon.c both
died with "too many #defines".  I'll try and post the fixes after
everything's complete, but here's what I did:

unixmain.c did a #include <fcntl.h> to get definitions for
O_RDWR, O_RDONLY, O_CREATE, and maybe one other O_*.  So I just
pulled those #defines out of fcntl.h and put them into unixmain.c
(packaged in a #ifdef TOO_MANY_DEFINES).

mon.c #include <ctype.h> for use with the INFERNO code, but only
does isupper().  SO I did a #define isupper(c) ( (c)>='A' && (c)<='Z').
It's not the world's most portable code, but it's enough, since the
one usage doesn't do anyting with side effects.

